Changed for Fak: adapted the per-position mask-before-verification ordering and
accepted-progress/rollback contract into a request-local Go constraint fork and
the ordinary host linear greedy verifier. No Python source is copied. Fak owns
its grammar implementations, target arithmetic and suffix eviction. Unlike
DeepInfer copy_without_status, the fork preserves the current grammar position.
The parent advances only through actually emitted tokens, including correction,
not the verifier's proposed or accepted-but-unemitted suffix. No XGrammar code,
CUDA sampler, stochastic verification or device-specific runtime is imported.

